// Cyrus R4 HUD and glyphs: the HUD design IR (`"kind":"hud"` files in assets/designs, same id space as the other
// designs). Honest limits, by construction: a vanilla client with a server-pushed resource pack can show TEXT in three
// places a server controls (the action bar line above the hotbar, boss bar titles, the scoreboard sidebar); a HUD here is
// glyph-based text in those three channels: small pixel-art glyphs in this mod's OWN font (`<ns>:hud`, a bitmap font +
// a space font for pixel offsets), bars made of glyph segments, values (health, food, XP, air, an ability's charges or
// cooldown, a boss's health) and plain text. NO core shaders, no free-form positioning, no widgets anywhere on screen
// (those need a client mod), no animation beyond the update rate. Glyph codepoints come from the project's glyph block
// (lib/cyrus/engine-core/identifiers.ts: the namespace's home block in the supplementary Private Use Area); since they
// live in the mod's own font they cannot clash with another pack's glyphs (the conflict engine still sees them).
